{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1510756-comparing-huntsmen-to-fae-touched","id":1510756,"title":"Comparing Huntsmen to Fae Touched","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-04T22:22:24-07:00","id":1510756,"title":"Comparing Huntsmen to Fae Touched","content":"This was something I noted on Discord a few months ago, but it's interesting to compare Huntsmen to Fae Touched for how similar they are.<br /> <br /> Out of all the fae of their own realms, Huntsmen and Fae Touched are the least empowered of their realms. While Huntsmen have a Wyrd score that can be pretty high on their own, and Fae Touched have access to Contracts, Huntsmen don't really have anything that uses Wyrd on its own, whereas Fae Touched <i>lacking</i> a Wyrd score means that their Contracts lack a lot of oomph and are slow to use. This means that they have to rely on being empowered by more typical/non fae means, namely Dread Powers* and Supernatural Merits and their own innate skills. While Hobs have access to Dread Powers, they have their own unique ones that not even Hobs have access to, much as Fae Touched can access particular merits only Fae Touched have access to on top of supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> They're both fae who can handle Iron as a normal object, and have no innate disadvantages to being struck by it. Sure, a Fae Touched will find their Contracts not working against it, but any damage from iron is because you got hit by a piece of metal, and not because the Gentry offended it and you're related to them.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, neither Huntsmen or Fae Touched suffer frailties of any variety. One could make an argument for the madness a Fae Touched suffers when they are subject to the Hedge as a form of a Frailty, but this doesn't follow the same rules as a normal frailty (where it can be suppressed with a Willpower). This is quite notable as Hobs and even Gentry suffer Frailties in turn (and it is likely from the Gentry themselves Frailties came to exist).<br /> <br /> While both are subject to <i>accepting</i> Oaths, neither Huntsmen or Fae Touched can <i>make</i> Oaths for the most part (Fae Touched can initiate them with Changelings). This stands in contrast to Hobs who can't make or accept them <i>at all</i> and Changelings and Gentry, who can make and accept them at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> And perhaps the most interesting parallel for me is that at the end of the day, a freed Huntsman and a Fae Touched have one parallel that stands as one of their most important things: a promise to a particular Changeling. To break that promise is something they cannot really conceive of for how important it is, and how it would hurt them. For a Fae Touched, it's the strength of that promise allowed them to become empowered in the first place, and the basis of many merits unique to them. For a Huntsman, the strength of that promise is what let them be freed at all, and breaking the oath would hurt them as much as it would any Changeling.<br /> <br /> *This isn't to say that Dread Powers aren't fae by their nature, but they are very much <i>old</i> fae, not the gentrified new fae methods.<br /> <br /> This isn't really meant to argue anything, just a thought that I had that I wanted to formalize somewhere that might introduce some discourse. Hope that people here find this interesting in one way or another, and thanks for reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}